    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:flxq4uyjfotciovpw3x3fxnu/app.bsky.feed.post/3mz7swluwac2w",
      "handle": "emollick.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Ethan Mollick",
      "text": "The Pro series of GPT models continues to be really impressive for one-shot problems that involve complex calculations, references, or sophisticated ideas.\n\nIt isn't particularly fast (or particularly pleasant) to use but GPT-6 Astra Pro gives that \"ask one question of the great oracle\" feel.",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/emollick.bsky.social/post/3mz7swluwac2w",
      "posted_at": "2026-11-01T02:59:51.629Z",
      "likes": 61,
      "replies": 3,
      "reposts": 2,
      "score": 6.1,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 1.8,
        "recency": 0.8,
        "age_hours": 30.7
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:flxq4uyjfotciovpw3x3fxnu/app.bsky.feed.post/3myzwg2oxgk25",
      "handle": "emollick.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Ethan Mollick",
      "text": "This is good advice from the Claude Code team (posted on X) for how to think about working with models like Opus 5.5.\n\nI would add: build checkpoints where the model reports back to you with interim ideas or prototypes so you can guide & give feedback, rather than one-shotting on your goal.",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/emollick.bsky.social/post/3myzwg2oxgk25",
      "posted_at": "2026-10-29T18:46:13.264Z",
      "likes": 174,
      "replies": 11,
      "reposts": 6,
      "score": 6.1,
      "score_parts": {
